# pdxsock -- caps.decl
#
# Format: R90-XREPO.013.M1-001 line-oriented caps.decl grammar
# (paideia-os design/architecture/caps-decl-format.md).
#
# `!KIND_FOO <mask>` = mandatory: exec fails -EACCES if the parent's
# cap-set does not hold at least this mask. ` KIND_FOO <mask>` (no
# `!`) = optional: narrowed to at most this mask, dropped to zero if
# the parent held none.
#
# pdxsock's role: netcat-adjacent general TCP/UDP client + server
# (paideia-os design/networking/r100-user-tools-plan.md §7). At v1.1-A
# the TCP client + TCP server paths are wired to the R72.M1-005
# (sysnos 87..94) socket syscall family; UDP client (sendto/recvfrom,
# sysnos 96/97) lands with pdxsock.M3-001 once R100-PREP-002's user
# surface stabilises. UDP server is out of scope per §7.2.
#
# Kind rationale:
#   KIND_USER          -- invoker attribution (audit record identity);
#                         every satellite in the R100 wave lists this.
#   KIND_TCP_SOCKET    -- mandatory here because both the client path
#                         (socket + connect + send + recv + shutdown)
#                         and the server path (socket + bind + listen +
#                         accept + recv + shutdown) fault without
#                         cap-slot 0 holding a TCP socket cap once
#                         sys_socket returns. The parent process (init /
#                         shell / a launcher) must have SEND (0x2) +
#                         RECV (0x1) + INVOKE (0x8) available or the
#                         first sys_send / sys_recv refuses with
#                         -EACCES.
#   KIND_UDP_SOCKET    -- optional at v1.1-A (UDP client body is a
#                         documented stub, per src/main.pdx's
#                         pdxsock_udp_not_yet path). Kept in the
#                         decl so the -u client path can be flipped
#                         from stub-to-real by src/*.pdx edits alone
#                         at M3-001, without a caps.decl churn.
#   KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT  -- optional; semantic-pipe emission is v1.1-B,
#                         a follow-on to this issue (paideia-os/pdxsock
#                         #16). Kept optional at v1.1-A so the ELF
#                         loads under a parent that has no semantic-
#                         pipe endpoint plumbed yet.

!KIND_USER               0x001   # invoker attribution (audit)
!KIND_TCP_SOCKET         0x00B   # READ (0x1) + SEND (0x2) + INVOKE (0x8)
 KIND_UDP_SOCKET         0x00B   # optional -- v1.1-A stub; M3-001 real
 KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT       0x001   # optional -- v1.1-B semantic-pipe
